# Railway functions and gateway

## What runs in production
- The **functions** Railway service runs `railway-stack/functions/server.mjs` on Node 22. It uses plain `node:http`, has no framework and no npm dependencies.
- Its `Dockerfile` copies only `package.json server.mjs qiAssistant.mjs`. **When you add a new `.mjs` module, add it to that `COPY` line**, or production will crash on import. Avoid npm dependencies; if one is truly needed, update the Dockerfile and say so.
- The health endpoint `GET /health` must keep returning 200; it is the Railway healthcheck in `railway.json`.

## Routes
- Add endpoints to the `routes` map in `server.mjs` as `'METHOD /path': handler`. The gateway strips `/functions/v1`, so the frontend URL `/functions/v1/send-email` arrives as `POST /send-email`.
- Current routes: `GET /health`, `POST /send-mrm-agenda`, `POST /send-email`, `POST /create-user`, `POST /delete-user`, `POST /qi-assistant`, and `GET|POST /osl/manak-pdf` (also `/api/osl/manak-pdf`, used by the extensions).
- Call `requireUser` on every user-facing endpoint. Reach PostgREST through the `rest` helper at `REST_URL` (internal `rest.railway.internal`) and GoTrue at `AUTH_URL`, using `SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` **server-side only**. Respond with the existing `json` / `corsJson` helpers.
- Never log secrets, JWTs or full request bodies that contain personal or client data.
- Email goes through Resend (`RESEND_API_KEY`, `EMAIL_FROM`) for the verified domains `qengineering.in` and `qirlpl.com`. Never send real email while testing.

## QI Assistant: keep the two copies in sync
- **Production QI Assistant = `railway-stack/functions/qiAssistant.mjs`** (`createQiAssistantHandler`, mounted at `POST /qi-assistant`). Changes to prompts, model handling or context building go here.
- `backend/supabase/functions/qi-assistant/index.ts` (plus `limsCrud.ts`) is the Deno version inherited from LIMS. It is **not deployed**, though it contains extra logic such as NOTEBOOK MODE (IS Code PDF text) and LIMS CRUD tools. Never assume a Deno-only feature works in production.
- When you change assistant behaviour, port it to `qiAssistant.mjs`. Mirror it in the Deno file only if that file holds the same logic, or else add a short `// NOTE: diverges from qiAssistant.mjs` comment. Mention any remaining divergence in your summary.
- Prompt changes should keep the rules: answer in the user's language, ground BIS facts in provided sources, and say "not found" instead of guessing.

## Gateway (`railway-stack/gateway/Caddyfile`)
- The CORS allowlist covers local Vite ports, `qengineering.in` / `www.qengineering.in` and the Railway frontend domains. A new frontend origin needs a matcher here.
- Keep the `header_down -Access-Control-*` stripping on each `reverse_proxy` to avoid duplicate CORS headers. Upstreams come from env (`GOTRUE_UPSTREAM`, `PGRST_UPSTREAM`, `STORAGE_UPSTREAM`, `FUNCTIONS_UPSTREAM`).

## Verify
- Run `node --check railway-stack/functions/server.mjs` and `node --check railway-stack/functions/qiAssistant.mjs`.
- Don't redeploy Railway services unless Amit asks. If a change needs a deploy, say which service (`functions`, `api`, ...) must be redeployed.
